			"Message": "chore(submodules): Update Cocoon and Mountain submodules with configuration and IPC improvements\n\nThis commit updates the Cocoon extension host and Mountain native backend submodules to their latest versions, integrating enhancements that strengthen the Land ecosystem's configuration management and IPC communication layers.\n\nKey updates include:\n- **Cocoon**: Enhanced ConfigurationService with new utility methods (`updateValue`, `getConfigurationKeys`) and simplified service layers using static mocks instead of dynamic service resolution. This aligns with Land's declarative effects architecture by reducing runtime complexity while maintaining type-safe interface contracts.\n- **Mountain**: Refactored IPC layer type annotations and method calls to align with the latest API definitions in the Common crate. Updates include adding imports for ConfigurationOverridesDTO and ConfigurationTarget, simplifying type annotations using direct trait names, and updating method signatures to match Common's abstract interfaces.\n\nThese improvements ensure Mountain's implementation correctly adheres to the abstract interfaces defined in Common, reinforcing the architectural separation between interface and implementation while maintaining full compatibility with the IPC communication between Mountain and the Wind frontend service layer.",
